 [{:title
   "Relocated :list-repositories stub in :services composition root collapses not-implemented into empty",
   :file "src/epiphany/infra/profile.clj",
   :detail
   "resolve-raw-adapters :services (profile.clj:67-69) wires real ADR-001 repository.edn read/write but keeps `:list-repositories (fn [] [])`. domain/status.clj:56 (query-registration-status) counts registered repos from this port, so a :services status query reports `:status :ok` with `:registered 0` even when repositories are registered — conflating 'not implemented' with 'empty', which ADR-004 §6 says must remain distinct, and sitting uneasily next to the profile contract's 'never a silent fallback' (AGENTS.md Local services). Provenance note: this exact stub predates 06cd710 (it lived in main.clj's per-command adapter maps, e.g. old make-status-adapters/make-ingest-adapters), so it is not introduced by this commit — but 06cd710 is the commit that promotes this map to the single sanctioned composition root and documents it as 'real adapters', which makes the stub look endorsed rather than placeholder. Not worth blocking promotion; worth a follow-up card either implementing a durable repo listing or throwing UNAVAILABLE from this fn.",
   :severity "nit",
   :card "eng-017n",
   :lens "architecture-law",
   :survives false,
   :reasons
   ["The claim is self-refuting on gating grounds and provenance grounds. (1) It explicitly concedes 'Not worth blocking promotion; worth a follow-up card' — under the review standard, a finding that cannot gate review→done is not a finding against this card. (2) Provenance confirmed: git log -S shows the `:list-repositories (fn [] [])` stub predates 06cd710 (present in ENG-003G fd20b30 and ENG-006C 2669d3b adapter maps), so it is grandfathered code this card relocated verbatim, not introduced. ENG-017N's scope was three bundled items: wiring the CLI through resolve-adapters (delivered), the write-op classifier guard (delivered), and law-harness generalization (delivered); implementing a durable repository listing was never in scope — no card in the delivery chain owns list-repositories yet (law/ports.clj types it `:any`, and only the in-memory adapter implements it for real). (3) The behavior is also bounded: `ep status` requires `--resource-id`, so the registration-stage count is per-repo context, and the 'registered 0' reading only arises if someone queries status without registration context — a known placeholder, not a silent fallback of the kind AGENTS.md prohibits (the profile contract's rule is about unreachable *services*, which :services does enforce with UNAVAILABLE for mongo-conn/index-dir). The right vehicle is exactly what the reviewer proposes — a follow-up card to implement durable repo listing or throw UNAVAILABLE — not a gate on ENG-017N."
    "The factual core is accurate (profile.clj:67-69 does wire `:list-repositories (fn [] [])` into the :services composition root, and domain/status.clj derives the registered count from that port), but this is not a finding against ENG-017N for three independent reasons. (1) Out of scope: the card's scope is exactly three items — wiring the CLI through the validating composition root, guarding the write-op classifier, and generalizing the law harness. Its acceptance criteria say nothing about implementing durable repository listing; no registry-listing port contract card exists yet, so this stub is grandfathered placeholder behavior, and the claim's own provenance note confirms it predates commit 06cd710 (it lived in main.clj's per-command adapter maps). (2) Self-declared non-gating: the reviewer rates it a 'nit' and explicitly states 'Not worth blocking promotion; worth a follow-up card' — a skeptic pass exists to gate review→done, and this claim concedes it does not gate. (3) The 'endorsed rather than placeholder' framing is weak: resolve-raw-adapters' docstring enumerates what :services composes (Mongo observations, Git-local repository.edn read/write metadata, Lucene index, Ollama embeddings) and does not claim a repository-listing capability; ADR-004 §6's not-implemented-vs-empty distinction is a real design tension but belongs to a future registration-listing card, not to this hardening bundle. Correct disposition: file the follow-up card the reviewer suggests (implement durable repo listing or throw UNAVAILABLE from :list-repositories), do not hold ENG-017N's promotion."]}
