   ["The claim is factually accurate — verified in the code: main.clj:453 binds index-ports via make-durable-index-ports unconditionally, and the :services branch (lines 461-476) discards it, passing :index-dir to profile/resolve-adapters which builds its own Lucene adapter (profile.clj:71). Git history (git log -L) shows commit 06cd710 (this card) removed the index-ports merge from the :services branch but left the unconditional binding, so it is code this card touched. However, the finding is self-classified as a nit and is not promotion-gating: the discarded construction's only side effect is Files/createDirectories on the same path (idempotent, immediately re-run by the profile-built adapter), there is no lock or correctness hazard (writers are per-call), and the fix is a one-line move of the let binding into the :local branch. The card's acceptance criteria (validating wrapper live on CLI paths, classifier guard, generalized law harness, green suite) are unaffected, and the docstring already states the index/projection relationship intent. A cosmetic dead binding in a private helper does not meet the bar for blocking a review→done promotion; it is appropriate as a follow-up tidy, not a gate."
