  {:title
   ":services composition now eagerly creates ~/.epiphany/index on commands that never use the index",
   :file "src/epiphany/infra/profile.clj",
   :detail
   "resolve-raw-adapters :services (lines 71-75) constructs the Lucene adapter, whose make-index-adapter runs Files/createDirectories at composition time (lucene.clj:196). After the retarget, `ep register -p services`, `ep inbox`, and `ep diff --seed-candidate` (via with-observations-adapter, main.clj:812-816) all create ~/.epiphany/index as a side effect despite never touching the index; on a read-only home these commands now fail where they previously succeeded. Marginal, but it is a behavior change introduced by the retarget that the card does not mention.",
   :severity "nit",
   :card "eng-017n",
   :lens "correctness",
   :survives false,
   :reasons
   ["Verified the code: the mechanics are accurate (profile.clj:71-75 does compose lucene/make-index-adapter, whose line 196 runs Files/createDirectories at construction, and register/status/inbox/diff -p services paths now flow through it). But this is refuted on three grounds. (1) Grandfathered behavior: the eager Files/createDirectories in make-index-adapter was introduced by ENG-003G (commits fd20b30/2573e7e), not this card — and pre-retarget paths like make-ingest-adapters and make-status-adapters :local already called make-durable-index-ports (same eager creation) at composition time, so eager index-dir creation on :local paths predates the retarget. (2) Documented and deliberate: the card's IMPLEMENTED comment explicitly states the retarget ('run-register, run-status, run-ingest, run-serve, with-observations-adapter all retargeted') and that ':services now composes real adapters ... durable Lucene index', and resolve-raw-adapters' docstring documents ':services returns real adapters (... on-disk Lucene index ...)'. Building the full port map eagerly at a composition root is the documented design; the card's whole deliverable is that production paths compose through resolve-adapters rather than hand-picking subsets of adapters. (3) Not promotion-gating: the effect only triggers on explicitly opted-in '-p services' (default :local uses in-memory adapters and creates nothing), already requires a reachable MongoDB, and the reviewer self-classifies severity as 'nit'/'marginal'. A nit against documented, deliberate composition-root behavior rooted in grandfathered adapter semantics does not gate a review→done promotion."
    "The mechanism is factually accurate — profile.clj:71-75 eagerly constructs lucene/make-index-adapter, and lucene.clj:196 runs Files/createDirectories at construction time, so :services-profile commands that never search (register, inbox-decide, diff --seed-candidate via with-observations-adapter, main.clj:812-816) do now create ~/.epiphany/index where the pre-retarget code (verified at 06cd710^: with-observations-adapter built only mongo/make-observations-adapter) did not. But the finding fails the promotion gate on three grounds: (1) It is self-classified as a nit/'marginal' — exactly the 'too minor to gate review→done' category. (2) The behavior is the direct, intended consequence of the card's explicit scope item 1: retarget the CLI onto profile/resolve-adapters, whose :services branch is specified (and documented in the IMPLEMENTED comment and the resolve-raw-adapters docstring) as composing the full real adapter map — Mongo observations, durable Lucene index, Ollama embeddings — with explicit :index-dir and UNAVAILABLE semantics. Eager composition at a composition root is the deliberate design, not an accident; making the index adapter lazy would be a separate refinement card. (3) The claimed failure mode (read-only home) only manifests under the :services profile, which by contract requires locally provisioned services (running MongoDB, Ollama) and explicit durable paths — a read-only home with a provisioned Mongo is a contrived environment for a dev-tool CLI whose whole purpose is durable writes. No acceptance criterion is violated and no correctness hole exists; not promotion-gating."]}]}
